<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Ergyng</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 950 CE (approx.) · capital Ariconium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small British kingdom in the Wye valley around the Roman town of Ariconium, whose name survives in Archenfield, a Welsh-speaking district of Herefordshire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ergyng emerged after Roman rule ended, its name derived from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariconium">Ariconium</a>, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-working">iron-working</a> town near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ross-on-wye">Ross-on-Wye</a>. It appears in the 6th and 7th centuries in the charters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-llandaff">Book of Llandaff</a>, which name local kings such as Peibio, associated in legend with the birth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubricius">Saint Dubricius</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ergyng was a Christian British kingdom in which churches and monasteries, many linked to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubricius">Dubricius</a>, held land through royal grants. Its rulers were at times linked to the dynasties of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gwent">Gwent</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-glywysing">Glywysing</a>. Little else is reliably known of its government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From the 7th century the kingdom was absorbed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gwent">Gwent</a>, and English settlement from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Mercia</a> advanced into the area. By the 10th century it was the district of Archenfield, under English lordship but still Welsh in law and speech; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domesday-book">Domesday Book</a> recorded its Welsh customs.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-ergyng.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Ergyng" width="320" height="335"><figcaption>Image: author of source image, plus my additions (myself) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wales.post-Roman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ariconium</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Peibio</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Welsh</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ergyng, Archenfield</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=725&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ergyng" aria-label="Kingdom of Ergyng on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4623 383 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Ergyng lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4943 639L4932 643"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4932 643h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4943 639h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4943 639h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ariconium. <a href="/atlas?year=725&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ergyng">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

